title:: Timeline limitations
categories:: Libraries>Param
summary:: Current limitations of the Param timeline system

section:: Can't always start in the middle of a clip

In classical DAW, timelines are a simple list of notes, but i made the choice to
allow patterns in timelines. Timelines are just regular supercollider patterns
under the hood. But patterns does not allow to say "start at the 10th second of
the pattern". Timelines include a system to unroll the pattern so you can start
it a any point. This can cause some delay if this is a big pattern. 
Unfortunately, there is no way to do that with Ndef, because on server side,
UGen graph can only start from the begining.

This is specificaly visible with ClipTimeline. You can start in the middle of a
Pdef, but you can't start in the middle of a Ndef, it will just play from the
start.

section:: Stopping can't stop currently playing events

Timelines are built on the supercollider pattern system. Currently I don't know
a way to stop a currently playing note when we stop the pattern that produced
it.

code::
Pdef(\aa, Pbind(\dur, 5)).play;
Pdef(\aa).stop; // prevent the next note from starting, but do not touch the current one 
::

This also apply to ClipTimeline, this means that when a Ndef clip is played and
you stop the ClipTimeline, the Ndef will continue to play its whole sustain
time.

NoteTimeline or Pdef clips doesn't suffer from this because under the hood, they
are embeded in the pattern. This means that the notes produced by the Pdef will
continue to play its whole sustain time, but the Pdef clip itself will stop and
not trigger the playing of the next Pdef notes.

section:: Undo/Redo system

Does not add history point when moving nodes to avoid cluttering the history.
Only adding/deleting nodes is recorded.
Does not handle track adding/deleting in ClipTimeline
